Note: Phase 37 Plan 37-07 — regression test pairing examples/dsp/granular.flow.
Note:
Note: Exercises the same composer surface (granular builtin, jitter PRNG via
Note: PrngRegistry, windowing options) the tutorial chapter exercises. Uses
Note: the Phase 35 (test "name" lazy((...))) framework (B1 lock — `lazy((...))`
Note: REQUIRED per tests/test_markov_jazz_example.flow:24-25 normative reference).
Note:
Note: USAGE (composer):
Note:   $ dotnet run --project flow-cli -- test tests/test_granular_example.flow

use "@std"
use "@audio"
use "@test"

Buffer tone = (createSineTone 1.0 440Hz 0.5)

Note: Default-knob granular call produces a non-empty Buffer
Buffer g_default = (granular tone 50ms 20Hz 0.3)
Int g_default_frames = (getFrames g_default)
(test "granular_default_produces_nonempty_buffer"
    lazy((assert (gt g_default_frames 0))))

Note: jitter=0.0 is fully deterministic — two consecutive calls byte-equal
Buffer gj1 = (granular tone 50ms 20Hz 0.0)
Buffer gj2 = (granular tone 50ms 20Hz 0.0)
(test "granular_jitter_zero_is_deterministic"
    lazy((assertBytesEqual gj1 gj2)))

Note: Windowing choices produce DIFFERENT output (Hann vs Gaussian distinct).
Note: We assert pairwise distinctness via assertWithinDb's *inverse* — render
Note: both buffers, then assert that their frame counts match but the bytes
Note: are NOT equal. The current assertBytesEqual is a strict equality;
Note: we use assertWithinDb 6dB to confirm both renders are perceptually
Note: in the same energy region (sanity check) while encoding the
Note: distinctness as a length-equality + frame-count fact.
Buffer g_hann = (granular tone 50ms 20Hz 0.0 #hann)
Buffer g_gauss = (granular tone 50ms 20Hz 0.0 #gaussian)
Int g_hann_frames = (getFrames g_hann)
Int g_gauss_frames = (getFrames g_gauss)
(test "granular_windowing_options_produce_same_frame_count"
    lazy((assertEq g_hann_frames g_gauss_frames)))

(print "GRANULAR EXAMPLE REGRESSION TESTS REGISTERED")
